## Evidence gaps I want the ledger to flag

Two facts would sharpen this brief materially and I could not source them in the time I had. The context packet already flagged both, but I want to double-underline that they matter to *my* argument specifically:

1. Whether the current MWAA design manual volumes have any acoustic performance criteria at all. My argument that "the tenant design manual is the acoustic standard" needs to know what is and isn't already in there.
2. Whether either airport has run a written PA governance policy or a silent-boarding pilot in the last ten years. My hospital-alarm analog would land harder against a documented MWAA experiment, positive or negative.

If either of those turns out to be already in the design manual and I've been arguing against a strawman, say so. The Strategist should update the framing accordingly.

